<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Log-Tek half yr shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>Log-Tek half yr shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Oct 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   9.4	   vs 7.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 3.0	   vs 2.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   1.11	  vs 0.72</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1.88	  vs 0.58</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.93	  vs 0.31</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.21	  vs 0.66</p>
<p>    Turnover		  35.44	 vs 32.06</p>
<p>Div payable Jan 31</p>
<p>on register Jan 10</p>
<p>Full name: Log-Tek Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  0.03	  vs 0.45</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the group was well focused and based on current trends they expected a material increase in earnings for the second six months.</p>
<p>Directors said talks with a black empowerment group, as cautioned about on July 29, were still in progress and shareholders were advised to be cautious dealing in the company's shares.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
